  "id": "dynamic-visual-display",
  "term": "dynamic visual display",
  "definition": "A dynamic visual display is a visual stimulus that changes over time, such as moving patterns that provide motion information. In this context, it refers to the changing visual scene whose spatiotemporal motion patterns help shape how an ambiguous event is perceived.",
